{
  "entry": "tokens.resolver.json",
  "spec": "Format 5 and 6: a token is an object with $value, and $-prefixed names are the spec's own. A member that is almost certainly one of them (value or $vlaue or $Value for $value, type for $type, $descripton for $description) is read as it, with an error naming what was meant, so the token is not lost or read as a group, and nothing that depends on it fails as well. A member named value that holds a token stays a child. A $-prefixed name near none of them is ignored with a warning. A member that would be a near miss of a property written properly beside it is not taken for it: the property wins, and the member is what it would be without this rule",
